{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf sv-freq [-h] [--vcf-input VCF_INPUT] [--gnomad-sv-file GNOMAD_SV_FILE]\n                              [--gnomad-lr-file GNOMAD_LR_FILE] [--min-overlap MIN_OVERLAP]\n                              [--max-distance MAX_DISTANCE]\n                              [--min-size-similarity MIN_SIZE_SIMILARITY] [--common-af COMMON_AF]\n                              [--rare-af RARE_AF]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --vcf-input VCF_INPUT\n                        Optional override for VCF input file.\n  --gnomad-sv-file GNOMAD_SV_FILE\n                        gnomAD-SV table (default: the library's, from 'ref gnomad-sv').\n  --gnomad-lr-file GNOMAD_LR_FILE\n                        gnomAD-LR table (default: the library's; GRCh38).\n  --min-overlap MIN_OVERLAP\n                        Minimum reciprocal overlap for same-type DEL/DUP/INV (default 0.5).\n  --max-distance MAX_DISTANCE\n                        Maximum insertion breakpoint distance, bp (default 500).\n  --min-size-similarity MIN_SIZE_SIMILARITY\n                        Minimum insertion size similarity (default 0.5).\n  --common-af COMMON_AF\n                        AF from which an SV is common (default 0.01).\n  --rare-af RARE_AF     AF below which an SV is rare (default 0.001).\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf sv-freq --vcf-input sniffles.vcf.gz\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  sv_freq_annotated.vcf.gz (+ .tbi) and sv_freq.tsv.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, bgzip, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also: samtools;\n  minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
